  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — What Counts as a Borrowing Cost" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Qualifying Assets" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Mandatory Capitalisation — No Expensing Option" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Conditions for Commencing Capitalisation" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Specific Borrowings — Actual Interest, Less Investment Income" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. General Borrowings — the Weighted Average Capitalisation Rate" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Suspension and Cessation of Capitalisation" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Capitalising Interest on a Specific Borrowing" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — Applying the Weighted Average Rate to General Borrowings" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IAS 23" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 借款费用 · Mandatory capitalisation for qualifying assets, converged with IAS 23's post-2007 approach · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Capitalising the cost of financing a qualifying asset</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 17 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of BORROWING COSTS — interest and OTHER costs an ENTERPRISE incurs in CONNECTION with the BORROWING of FUNDS — REQUIRING CAPITALISATION of BORROWING costs DIRECTLY attributable to the ACQUISITION, construction, or PRODUCTION of a QUALIFYING asset, CONSISTENT with IAS 23's OWN current (post-2007) approach internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — What Counts as a Borrowing Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Interest, discount/premium amortisation, ancillary costs, and certain exchange differences</div><div class="principle">BORROWING costs WITHIN this Standard's SCOPE include INTEREST expense, AMORTISATION of DISCOUNTS or PREMIUMS on BORROWINGS, ANCILLARY costs INCURRED in CONNECTION with ARRANGING borrowings, and EXCHANGE differences on FOREIGN currency borrowings TO THE EXTENT they REPRESENT an ADJUSTMENT to INTEREST costs.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Qualifying Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Assets requiring a substantial period to prepare for use or sale</div><div class="text-supporting">A "QUALIFYING ASSET" is an ASSET that NECESSARILY requires a SUBSTANTIAL period of TIME to get READY for its INTENDED use or SALE — TYPICALLY fixed ASSETS under construction, INVESTMENT property under CONSTRUCTION, or LARGE inventories REQUIRING an EXTENDED production PROCESS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Mandatory Capitalisation — No Expensing Option</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Capitalisation is required, not elective</div><div class="text-supporting">BORROWING costs DIRECTLY attributable to a QUALIFYING asset MUST be CAPITALISED as PART of the asset's COST — THERE is NO option to SIMPLY expense SUCH costs as INCURRED, CONSISTENT with IAS 23's OWN elimination of its FORMER expensing option (WHICH was REMOVED in a 2007 revision INTERNATIONALLY, ALIGNING the two frameworks).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Conditions for Commencing Capitalisation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">All three conditions must be met simultaneously</div><div class="check-list"><span>Asset expenditures have been incurred</span><span>Borrowing costs have been incurred</span><span>Activities necessary to prepare the asset for its intended use or sale are in progress</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Specific Borrowings — Actual Interest, Less Investment Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Netting off any temporary investment returns</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE FUNDS are BORROWED SPECIFICALLY for the PURPOSE of OBTAINING a QUALIFYING asset, the AMOUNT of BORROWING costs ELIGIBLE for CAPITALISATION is the ACTUAL borrowing COSTS incurred on THAT specific BORROWING DURING the period, LESS any INVESTMENT income EARNED on the TEMPORARY investment of ANY unused BORROWED funds.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>General Borrowings — the Weighted Average Capitalisation Rate</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Applying a blended rate to the excess expenditure</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ENTERPRISE uses GENERAL (RATHER than SPECIFIC) borrowings to FUND a QUALIFYING asset, the AMOUNT to CAPITALISE is DETERMINED by APPLYING a WEIGHTED AVERAGE capitalisation RATE (based on the ENTERPRISE'S general BORROWINGS outstanding DURING the period) to the PORTION of asset EXPENDITURES that EXCEEDS any SPECIFIC borrowings DIRECTLY related to THAT asset.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Suspension and Cessation of Capitalisation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Pausing during extended interruptions, stopping once the asset is ready</div><div class="text-supporting">CAPITALISATION is SUSPENDED DURING extended PERIODS in WHICH active DEVELOPMENT of the QUALIFYING asset is INTERRUPTED, and CEASES ENTIRELY once the ASSET is SUBSTANTIALLY ready for its INTENDED use or SALE — AT which POINT any FURTHER borrowing costs are SIMPLY expensed as INCURRED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Capitalising Interest on a Specific Borrowing</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Netting off temporary investment income</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A dedicated construction loan</div><div class="wk-body">A company borrows RMB 100,000,000 specifically to fund the construction of a new factory, incurring RMB 6,000,000 of interest during the year. Unused funds were temporarily invested, earning RMB 400,000 of investment income.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company CAPITALISES RMB 6,000,000 − RMB 400,000 = <strong>RMB 5,600,000</strong> as PART of the factory's COST, with the REMAINDER of any OTHER unrelated interest expensed AS incurred.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying the Weighted Average Rate to General Borrowings</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Capitalising a blended rate on the excess expenditure</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Funding a qualifying asset from a general borrowing pool</div><div class="wk-body">A company spends RMB 50,000,000 on a qualifying asset during the year, with no specific borrowing attached. The company's weighted average capitalisation rate on its general borrowings is 5%.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company CAPITALISES RMB 50,000,000 × 5% = <strong>RMB 2,500,000</strong> of borrowing COSTS as PART of the asset's COST, DETERMINED using the WEIGHTED AVERAGE rate ACROSS its GENERAL borrowing POOL.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 17 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Amount of borrowing costs capitalised during the period</span><span>Capitalisation rate used to determine borrowing costs eligible for capitalisation on general borrowings</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an asset genuinely qualifies as requiring a substantial period to prepare for use</span><span>When capitalisation should be suspended or ceased</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Weighted average capitalisation rate for general borrowings</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 23</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 17 vs IAS 23</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 17</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 23</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Capitalisation requirement</span><span>MANDATORY for qualifying assets</span><span>MANDATORY for qualifying assets — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Weighted average rate for general borrowings</span><span>Required</span><span>Required — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — the MANDATORY capitalisation APPROACH mirrors IAS 23's OWN post-2007 international POSITION closely.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every borrowing cost event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Capitalised borrowing costs</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Added to the qualifying asset's cost</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Non-capitalised borrowing costs</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed as incurred, once capitalisation ceases</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 4</span><span>Fixed Assets — the primary asset category into which capitalised borrowing costs are typically added</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Qualifying asset</div><div class="glossary-def">An asset that necessarily requires a substantial period of time to get ready for its intended use or sale.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Weighted average capitalisation rate</div><div class="glossary-def">A blended interest rate, derived from an enterprise's general borrowings, applied to the portion of qualifying asset expenditure not funded by specific borrowings.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe17 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
